  "note": "Independent re-judgment at HEAD (audit-b). RFC 8955 Section 4.2: \"All combinations of components within a single Flow Specification are allowed. However, some combinations cannot match any packets (e.g., \"ICMP Type AND Port\" will never match any packets) and thus SHOULD NOT be propagated by BGP.\" All 12 tags across core CheckMatchable, flowspec plugin origination (config route + update text), RIB receive-side retention-but-ineligibility (and withdrawal), and ze config validate .ci prove unmatchable type/value combinations are refused on origination and retained ineligible (never propagated/installed) on receipt, paired with closest matchable positive controls.",
